{
  "name": "LEARN — Expert Output",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Captures lessons from Expert stage outputs into the Shared Brain (lessons_learned.md only).",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": ["**/1_Expert/logic_explanation*.md", "**/1_Expert/test_plan*.md"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "LEARN phase (lightweight) — Expert output.\n\nA new Expert file has been created. Your job is to check if it contains any knowledge worth saving to the Shared Brain.\n\nRead the newly created file. Look only for the following — do not invent findings:\n- Ticket structure problems or missing acceptance criteria that caused ambiguity during the Expert stage\n- Module dependencies or relationships that the Expert had to figure out that are not already documented in project_context.md\n- Framework or tooling constraints discovered during this ticket\n\nFor each genuine finding:\n1. Open lessons_learned.md and scan for a similar existing entry. If a similar entry already exists, skip this finding entirely.\n2. If the finding is genuinely new, append one line to lessons_learned.md using this exact format:\n   [DATE] [TICKET-ID] [LOGGED] [FRAMEWORK] — {concise lesson in one sentence}\n\nRules:\n- Do NOT evaluate any finding for promotion to product.md\n- Do NOT modify pattern_registry.md\n- Do NOT modify project_context.md\n- Do NOT rewrite or edit existing entries\n- If nothing new is found, do nothing and do not write anything"
  }
}
